  #line-at(264.41pt, 365.45pt, " on 6° off-axis sapphire is shown in Figure 7 (a). The film ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 379.25pt, "exhibited elongated surface features aligned with the off-cut direction, which is characteristic of a ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 393.05pt, "step-assisted deposition mode. This behavior has been reported previously for LPCVD β-Ga₂O₃ ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 406.85pt, "on vicinal sapphire ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 8.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(172.1pt, 402.29pt, "15,16")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(190.37pt, 406.85pt, ", where the increased density of atomic steps suppress random island ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 420.67pt, "nucleation, reduce rotational domain formation, and support more coherent lateral ordering. SPE ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 434.47pt, "pseudo-substrate sample followed the expected deposition behavior on the vicinal surface and ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 448.27pt, "yielded a mobility of 45 cm²/V·s at a bulk carrier concentration of 1.3 × 10¹⁷ cm⁻³, which aligned ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 462.07pt, "with the transport behavior associated with step-flow-facilitated deposition on 6° off-axis sapphire.  ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 475.87pt, "The XRD results, shown in Figure 7 (b), further support these observations. The LPCVD-grown ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 489.67pt, "β-Ga")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 8.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(96.024pt, 490.63pt, "2")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(100.1pt, 489.67pt, "O")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 8.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(108.74pt, 490.63pt, "3")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(112.82pt, 489.67pt, " film on bare miscut sapphire displayed parasitic peaks, whereas the film on the SPE ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 503.47pt, "template exhibited dominant β-Ga")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 8.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(238.25pt, 504.43pt, "2")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(242.33pt, 503.47pt, "O")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 8.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(250.97pt, 504.43pt, "3")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(255.05pt, 503.47pt, " (−201), (−402), (−603), and (−804) reflections along with ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 517.27pt, "the sapphire (006) peak. For the film on the SPE template, additional weak polycrystalline peaks ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 531.07pt, "were detected, consistent with the SEM morphology that revealed faceting and mixed-phase ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 544.87pt, "regions. However, these peaks were of very low intensity compared to the dominant (−201) ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 558.67pt, "reflection, indicating that they originate from a thin fraction near the film surface. Further LPCVD ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 572.47pt, "optimization is planned to suppress these features and achieve uniform single-phase films, in order ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 586.3pt, "to further improve the film morphology and carrier mobility.  ")
]

